---
import { ChineseRestaurantExperience } from "../components/chinese-restraurant/ChineseRestaurantExperience";
import ProjectWrapper from "../components/ProjectWrapper.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ElainesSoupCard from "../projects/soup-card/components/ElainesSoupCard";

// Welcome to Astro! Wondering what to do next? Check out the Astro documentation at https://docs.astro.build
// Don't want to use any of this? Delete everything in this file, the `assets`, `components`, and `layouts` directories, and start fresh.
---

<Layout>
  <ProjectWrapper
    name="The Waitlist"
    episodeName="The Chinese Restaurant"
    season={2}
    episode={11}
  >
    <Fragment slot="note">
      <p>
        In <em>The Chinese Restaurant</em>, Jerry, Elaine, and George stop for
        dinner before a movie. They're told the wait will be “five, ten
        minutes.”
      </p>
      <p>
        What follows is a string of missed signals, parties seated ahead of
        them, and a mangled name.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the end, their table becomes ready, but not before they leave the
        restaurant in frustration.
      </p>
      <p>
        This interactive waitlist brings some of that absurdity into an
        interface inspired by Apple's Dynamic Island.
      </p>
      <p>I hope you enjoy playing with it.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <ChineseRestaurantExperience client:visible />
  </ProjectWrapper>

  <ProjectWrapper
    name="Elaine's Soup Card"
    episodeName="The Soup Nazi"
    season={7}
    episode={6}
  >
    <Fragment slot="note">
      <p>
        In <em>The Soup Nazi</em>, we meet a local business owner who treats
        buying his soup as a privilege. His strict rules around ordering earn
        him an infamous nickname.
      </p>
      <p>
        He serves the best soup in town, but you have to follow a rigid ordering
        routine. One misstep, and it might be "No soup for you!"
      </p>

      <p>
        This interactive membership card imagines what that kind of system might
        look like if someone actually bothered to formalize it, featuring his
        greatest nemesis: Elaine.
      </p>

      <p>
        It turns the shop's ridiculous rules into a piece of equally ridiculous
        bureaucracy that shows just how close Elaine is to getting banned.
      </p>
      <p>I hope you enjoy playing with it.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <ElainesSoupCard client:visible />
  </ProjectWrapper>
</Layout>
